  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Model & Protocol:\n      - Fully eliminated all dynamic allocations during request parsing.\n      - Rebuilt the entire parsing pipeline using Span<T>, pooled buffers, and zero‑copy slicing.\n      - Removed all intermediate strings, temporary arrays, and transient objects.\n      - Achieved a completely allocation‑free request lifecycle with deterministic memory behavior.\n      - Protocol layer fully isolated and “frozen”; no server‑specific logic remains inside the protocol.\n      - Unified all WebSocket send operations into a single low‑level API: MulticastData(...).\n      - Protocol now handles only frame construction, opcode handling, and multicast dispatch.\n      - Server implementations can expand freely without requiring any protocol modifications.",
